The API starts from the destructive `000000000001` baseline. Use it only for an
empty schema; an existing database already stamped at that revision advances
through the child migrations with `alembic upgrade head`. The baseline and the
Calculation migration do not support downgrade recovery.

Before applying `000000000002_calculations` to an existing database, take a
database backup and record the legacy row counts:

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS designer_model_rows FROM designer_models;
SELECT COUNT(*) AS predictor_model_rows FROM predictor_models;
```

The migration conditionally drops those two tables and creates `calculations`.
It intentionally does not delete objects referenced by legacy `model_url`
values, so any object-store cleanup is a separate, explicit operation after the
backup and retention policy have been confirmed.
